# {{lb|en|business|economics}} That which is [[produce]]d, then [[trade]]d, bought or sold, then finally [[consume]]d and consists of an [[action]] or [[work]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1840|author=[[w:Martin Van Buren|Martin Van Buren]]|title=Fourth State of the Union Address|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Martin_Van_Buren%27s_Fourth_State_of_the_Union_address
|text=The acts of Congress establishing new mail routes and requiring more expensive '''services''' on others and the increasing wants of the country have for three years past carried the expenditures something beyond the accruing revenues, the excess having been met until the past year by the surplus which had previously accumulated.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1950|author=81st Congress of the United States|title=Public Law 81-774: Defense Production Act of 1950|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Defense_Production_Act_of_1950
|text=To establish a system of priorities and allocations for materials and facilities, authorize the requisitioning thereof, provide financial assistance for expansion of productive capacity and supply, provide for price and wage stabilization, provide for the settlement of labor disputes, strengthen controls over credit, and by these measures facilitate the production of goods and '''services''' necessary for the national security, and for other purposes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987-10-29|author=[[w:Ronald Reagan|Ronald Reagan]]|title=Executive Order 12613: Prohibiting Imports from Iran|section=1|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Executive_Order_12613
|text=Except as otherwise provided in regulations issued pursuant to this Order, no goods or '''services''' of Iranian origin may be imported into the United States, including its territories and possessions, after the effective date of this Order.}}
